WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.900
What happens when the flight computer itself freezes?

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.020
If the failsafe is software, it freezes too

3
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.120
D100 puts the rescue in hardware.

4
00:00:10.254 --> 00:00:13.934
Inertial sensors and the radio link reach two flight cores,

5
00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:19.314
one flying the drone and one navigating, in hard real time.

6
00:00:19.314 --> 00:00:22.782
Cameras feed a pose engine made of geometry rather than a trained

7
00:00:22.782 --> 00:00:26.982
network, so it keeps working with no satellite signal at all.

8
00:00:26.982 --> 00:00:30.082
Camera features and inertial data fuse into a full pose,

9
00:00:30.082 --> 00:00:34.722
30 times a second, delivered straight to the flight loop.

10
00:00:34.722 --> 00:00:38.383
In normal flight, the motor commands leave on eight channels to the

11
00:00:38.383 --> 00:00:39.483
speed controllers.

12
00:00:39.983 --> 00:00:42.803
That path trusts the flight cores to be running.

13
00:00:42.884 --> 00:00:47.064
The failsafe island runs on its own power and its own clock.

14
00:00:47.064 --> 00:00:50.984
It notices a lost link, lost GPS or a sensor fault in

15
00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:54.464
hardware, and picks return or land.

16
00:00:54.464 --> 00:00:57.944
Then it drives the speed controllers directly, without the flight computer.

17
00:00:58.244 --> 00:01:01.864
This is a structure, not a proven result.

18
00:01:01.864 --> 00:01:05.882
No D100 silicon has been made or measured.

19
00:01:05.882 --> 00:01:10.242
An FPGA validates the design, and every figure is a target

20
00:01:11.322 --> 00:01:13.982
Bring us your mission and your failure cases.

21
00:01:13.982 --> 00:01:17.382
We will tell you what D100 must prove.
